{"title": "Sectional Mock #67 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>What is the simplified form of [<sup>3</sup>&radic;64 * <sup>3/2</sup>&radic;27 &div; <sup>5/2</sup>&radic;32 * &radic;729]?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>[<sup>3</sup>&radic;64 * <sup>3/2</sup>&radic;27 &div; <sup>5/2</sup>&radic;32 * &radic;729] &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["2<sup>2</sup> * 3<sup>3</sup>", "3<sup>5</sup>", "2<sup>5</sup>", "2<sup>3</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["2<sup>2</sup> * 3<sup>3</sup>", "3<sup>5</sup>", "2<sup>5</sup>", "2<sup>3</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>= [<sup>3</sup>&radic;64 * <sup>3/2</sup>&radic;27 &div; <sup>5/2</sup>&radic;32 * &radic;729]</p><p>= [<sup>3</sup>&radic;(2<sup>6</sup>) * <sup>3/2</sup>&radic;(3<sup>3</sup>) &div; <sup>5/2</sup>&radic;(2<sup>5</sup>) * &radic;(3<sup>6</sup>)]</p><p>= [2<sup>6 * (1/3)</sup> * 3<sup>3 * (2/3)</sup> &div; 2<sup>5 * (2/5)</sup> * 3<sup>6 * (1/2)</sup>]</p><p>= [2<sup>2</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup> &div; 2<sup>2</sup> * 3<sup>3</sup>]</p><p>= 3<sup>2</sup> * 3<sup>3</sup></p><p>= 3<sup>5</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>= [<sup>3</sup>&radic;64 * <sup>3/2</sup>&radic;27 &div; <sup>5/2</sup>&radic;32 * &radic;729]</p><p>= [<sup>3</sup>&radic;(2<sup>6</sup>) * <sup>3/2</sup>&radic;(3<sup>3</sup>) &div; <sup>5/2</sup>&radic;(2<sup>5</sup>) * &radic;(3<sup>6</sup>)]</p><p>= [2<sup>6 * (1/3)</sup> * 3<sup>3 * (2/3)</sup> &div; 2<sup>5 * (2/5)</sup> * 3<sup>6 * (1/2)</sup>]</p><p>= [2<sup>2</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup> &div; 2<sup>2</sup> * 3<sup>3</sup>]</p><p>= 3<sup>2</sup> * 3<sup>3</sup></p><p>= 3<sup>5</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the unit digit in (999)<sup>253</sup> + (642)<sup>87</sup>  X  (305)<sup>44</sup>.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>(999)<sup>253</sup> + (642)<sup>87</sup> X (305)<sup>44</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["8", "0", "1", "9"], "options_hi": ["8", "0", "1", "9"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>&bull; (999)<sup>253</sup> &rarr; last digit 9; odd exponent &rarr; 9</p><p>&bull; (642)<sup>87</sup> &rarr; last digit 2; cycle of 2 is [2,4,8,6]; 87/4 = 3 (remainder) &rarr; 2<sup>3</sup> = 8</p><p>&bull; (305)<sup>44</sup> &rarr; last digit 5 &rarr; cycle of 5 is always 5</p><p>&bull; Unit digit = 9 + 8 * 5 = 9 + 40 = 9</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&bull; (999)<sup>253</sup> &rarr; last digit 9; odd exponent &rarr; 9</p><p>&bull; (642)<sup>87</sup> &rarr; last digit 2; cycle of 2 is [2,4,8,6]; 87/4 = 3 (remainder) &rarr; 2<sup>3</sup> = 8</p><p>&bull; (305)<sup>44</sup> &rarr; last digit 5 &rarr; cycle of 5 is always 5</p><p>&bull; Unit digit = 9 + 8 * 5 = 9 + 40 = 9</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 9(a<sup>2</sup> +b<sup>2</sup>) +c<sup>2</sup> + 20 = 12(a +2b), then the value of &radic;(6a + 9b + 2c) is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 9(a<sup>2</sup> +b<sup>2</sup>) +c<sup>2</sup> + 20 = 12(a +2b) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &radic;(6a + 9b + 2c) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["4", "3", "6", "2"], "options_hi": ["4", "3", "6", "2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>9(a<sup>2</sup> +b<sup>2</sup>) +c<sup>2</sup> + 20 = 12(a +2b)</p><p>9a<sup>2</sup> + 9b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> + 20  -  12a  -  24b = 0</p><p>9a<sup>2</sup>  -  12a + 4 + 9b<sup>2</sup>  -  24b + 16 + c<sup>2</sup> = 0</p><p>(3a  -  2)<sup>2</sup> + (3b  -  4)<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> = 0</p><p>Sum of squares will only be zero when they are individually zero.</p><p>3a  -  2 = 0 =&gt; a = 2/3</p><p>3b  -  4 = 0 =&gt; b = 4/3</p><p>c<sup>2</sup> = 0 =&gt; c = 0</p><p>Now,</p><p><img width=89 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=152 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image034.png\"></p><p><img width=89 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image035.png\"></p><p><img width=25 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image036.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>9(a<sup>2</sup> +b<sup>2</sup>) +c<sup>2</sup> + 20 = 12(a +2b)</p><p>9a<sup>2</sup> + 9b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> + 20  -  12a  -  24b = 0</p><p>9a<sup>2</sup>  -  12a + 4 + 9b<sup>2</sup>  -  24b + 16 + c<sup>2</sup> = 0</p><p>(3a  -  2)<sup>2</sup> + (3b  -  4)<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> = 0</p><p>Sum of squares will only be zero when they are individually zero.</p><p>3a  -  2 = 0 =&gt; a = 2/3</p><p>3b  -  4 = 0 =&gt; b = 4/3</p><p>c<sup>2</sup> = 0 =&gt; c = 0</p><p>Now,</p><p><img width=89 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=152 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image034.png\"></p><p><img width=89 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image035.png\"></p><p><img width=25 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19954/image036.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>P and Q started a business with investment in the ratio 8: 13 respectively. After 3 months, P added 22.5% to his capital and after next 3 months, Q withdrew 20% from his capital. If they together earned Rs.2105 as profit in one year, then the share of P in profit is Rs.__.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 8: 13 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; 3 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, P &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 22.5% &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2375; 3 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, Q &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; 20% &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 2105 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; P &#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; ______&#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["935", "900", "1035", "1000"], "options_hi": ["935", "900", "1035", "1000"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the investment of P and Q are 8a and 13a respectively. Then,</p><p>Profit ratio, P: Q = (3 * 8a + (12  -  3) * (100 + 22.5)% of 8a): (6 * 13a + (12  -  6) * (100  -  20)% of 13a)</p><p>= 187: 234</p><p>Total profit earned = Rs.2105</p><p>Then, share of P in profit = 2105 * 187/(187 + 234)</p><p>= <b>Rs.935</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the investment of P and Q are 8a and 13a respectively. Then,</p><p>Profit ratio, P: Q = (3 * 8a + (12  -  3) * (100 + 22.5)% of 8a): (6 * 13a + (12  -  6) * (100  -  20)% of 13a)</p><p>= 187: 234</p><p>Total profit earned = Rs.2105</p><p>Then, share of P in profit = 2105 * 187/(187 + 234)</p><p>= <b>Rs.935</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Speed of a flight is 200 km/hr. It covers a certain distance in 56 hours. Find the time taken to cover the same distance at 250 km/hr.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; 200 km/hr &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2361; 56 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 250 km/hr &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["42.9 hours", "40.4 hours", "44.8 hours", "50.6 hours"], "options_hi": ["42.9 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "40.4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "44.8 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "50.6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Distance travelled by flight in 56 hours = 56 * 200 = 11200 km</p><p>Required time = 11200/250 = 44.8 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Distance travelled by flight in 56 hours = 56 * 200 = 11200 km</p><p>Required time = 11200/250 = 44.8 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 12: 18 :: p: 48 and (p  -  12): (p  -  2) :: (q + 6): (q + 27), then what is the value of 'q'?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 12: 18 :: p: 48 &#2324;&#2352; (p - 12): (p - 2) :: (q + 6): (q + 27) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 'q' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["30", "32", "34", "36"], "options_hi": ["30", "32", "34", "36"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question:</p><p>12: 18 :: p: 48</p><p>12 * 48 = p * 18</p><p>p = 32</p><p>Now, (p  -  12): (p  -  2) :: (q + 6): (q + 27)</p><p>(32  -  12): (32  -  2) :: (q + 6): (q + 27)</p><p>20 * (q + 27) = (q + 6) * 30</p><p><b>q = 36</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question:</p><p>12: 18 :: p: 48</p><p>12 * 48 = p * 18</p><p>p = 32</p><p>Now, (p  -  12): (p  -  2) :: (q + 6): (q + 27)</p><p>(32  -  12): (32  -  2) :: (q + 6): (q + 27)</p><p>20 * (q + 27) = (q + 6) * 30</p><p><b>q = 36</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum of &#8377;1,456, when invested for ten years, amounts to &#8377;2,366 on maturity. Find the rate of simple interest per annum that was to be paid on the sum invested.</p>", "q_hi": "1,456 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2360; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2346;&#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2340;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352; 2,366 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["5.75%", "6.5%", "6.25%", "6.15%"], "options_hi": ["5.75%", "6.5%", "6.25%", "6.15%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Here Pricipal amount = Rs 1456</p><p>Time= 10 years</p><p>Amount = Rs 2366</p><p>Amount =P*R*T/100 + P</p><p>2366 = 1456*R*10/100 + 1456</p><p>1456(R/10 +1)=2366</p><p>(R/10 +1)=2366/1456=1.625</p><p>R=6.25%</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here Pricipal amount = Rs 1456</p><p>Time= 10 years</p><p>Amount = Rs 2366</p><p>Amount =P*R*T/100 + P</p><p>2366 = 1456*R*10/100 + 1456</p><p>1456(R/10 +1)=2366</p><p>(R/10 +1)=2366/1456=1.625</p><p>R=6.25%</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Trapezium MNOP is shown in figure where MN || OP and length of parallel sides are 12 cm and 17 cm respectively. Find the length of diagonal PN of the trapezium if area of trapezium is 72.5 cm<sup>2</sup>.</p><p><img width=248 height=118 id=\"Picture 18\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3147/image006.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348; MNOP &#2325;&#2379; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2306; MN || OP &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 12 &#2360;&#2375;.&#2350;&#2368;. &#2324;&#2352; 17 &#2360;&#2375;.&#2350;&#2368;. &#2361;&#2376; | &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 72.5 &#2360;&#2375;.&#2350;&#2368;.<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; PN &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; |</p><p><img width=248 height=118 id=\"Picture 18\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3147/image006.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["12 cm", "13 cm", "14 cm", "15 km"], "options_hi": ["12 &#2360;&#2375;.&#2350;&#2368;.", "13 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "14 &#2360;&#2375;.&#2350;&#2368;.", "15 &#2360;&#2375;.&#2350;&#2368;."], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Draw a line NA perpendicular to OP.</p><p><img width=248 height=118 id=\"Picture 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3147/image007.png\"></p><p>Area of trapezium = &frac12; * (Sum of parallel sides) * (Perpendicular distance between parallel sides)</p><p>=&gt; 72.5 = &frac12; * (12 + 17) * NA</p><p>=&gt; NA = 145/29 = 5 cm</p><p>MNAP is a rectangle-</p><p>=&gt; PN<sup>2</sup> = MN<sup>2</sup> + NA<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; PN<sup>2</sup> = 12<sup>2</sup> + 5<sup>2</sup> = 144 + 25 = 169</p><p>=&gt; PN = 13 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Draw a line NA perpendicular to OP.</p><p><img width=248 height=118 id=\"Picture 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3147/image007.png\"></p><p>Area of trapezium = &frac12; * (Sum of parallel sides) * (Perpendicular distance between parallel sides)</p><p>=&gt; 72.5 = &frac12; * (12 + 17) * NA</p><p>=&gt; NA = 145/29 = 5 cm</p><p>MNAP is a rectangle-</p><p>=&gt; PN<sup>2</sup> = MN<sup>2</sup> + NA<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; PN<sup>2</sup> = 12<sup>2</sup> + 5<sup>2</sup> = 144 + 25 = 169</p><p>=&gt; PN = 13 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the volume of the wall of a hollow sphere having external and internal radius, 11cm and 8cm respectively.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 11 cm &#2324;&#2352; 8 cm &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2352;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2379;&#2326;&#2354;&#2375; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; .</p>", "options_en": ["1092&#960; cubic cm", "3432&#960; cubic cm", "2760&#960; cubic cm", "<i> </i>1449&#960; cubic cm"], "options_hi": ["1092&#960; &#2328;&#2344; cm", "3432&#960; &#2328;&#2344; cm", "2760&#960; &#2328;&#2344; cm", "<i> </i>1449&#960; &#2328;&#2344; cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>According to the Question,</p><p>External and internal radius of the wall of a hollow sphere = 11 cm and 8 cm respectively</p><p>We know, volume of a sphere = <img width=33 height=35 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18087/image004.png\" ></p><p>Volume of the wall of sphere = <img width=90 height=38 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18087/image005.png\" ></p><p>= <img width=107 height=33 id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18087/image006.png\" ></p><p>=<img width=63 height=33 id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18087/image007.png\" ></p><p>=<img width=55 height=12 id=\"Picture 13\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18087/image008.png\" ></p><p>=<i> </i><img width=103 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18087/image009.png\">Ans.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the Question,</p><p>External and internal radius of the wall of a hollow sphere = 11 cm and 8 cm respectively</p><p>We know, volume of a sphere = <img width=33 height=35 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18087/image004.png\" ></p><p>Volume of the wall of sphere = <img width=90 height=38 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18087/image005.png\" ></p><p>= <img width=107 height=33 id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18087/image006.png\" ></p><p>=<img width=63 height=33 id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18087/image007.png\" ></p><p>=<img width=55 height=12 id=\"Picture 13\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18087/image008.png\" ></p><p>=<i> </i><img width=103 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18087/image009.png\">Ans.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a<sup>x</sup> = b, b<sup>y</sup> = c and c<sup>z</sup> = a<sup>2</sup>, then what is the value of xyz?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a<sup>x</sup> = b, b<sup>y</sup> = c &#2324;&#2352; c<sup>z</sup> = a<sup>2</sup>, &#2340;&#2379; xyz &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["2", "-1", "0", "1"], "options_hi": ["2", "-1", "0", "1"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>It is given that, c<sup>z</sup> = a<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; (b<sup>y</sup>)<sup>z</sup> = c<sup>z</sup> = a<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; (a<sup>x</sup>)<sup>yz</sup> = a<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; a<sup>xyz</sup> = a<sup>2</sup></p><p>Hence, xyz = 2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>It is given that, c<sup>z</sup> = a<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; (b<sup>y</sup>)<sup>z</sup> = c<sup>z</sup> = a<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; (a<sup>x</sup>)<sup>yz</sup> = a<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; a<sup>xyz</sup> = a<sup>2</sup></p><p>Hence, xyz = 2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>In &#916;PQR, if PT is the median, then which of the following is correct?</p>", "q_hi": "'PQR' &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; PT &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?", "options_en": ["PQ<sup>2</sup> + PR<sup>2</sup> = PT<sup>2</sup> + QR<sup>2</sup>", "PQ<sup>2</sup> + PR<sup>2</sup> = 2(PT<sup>2</sup> + QT<sup>2</sup>)", "PQ<sup>2</sup> + PR<sup>2</sup> = 2(PT<sup>2</sup> - QR<sup>2</sup>)", "PQ<sup>2</sup> + PR = PT<sup>2</sup> + QT<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["PQ<sup>2</sup> + PR<sup>2</sup> = PT<sup>2</sup> + QR<sup>2</sup>", "PQ<sup>2</sup> + PR<sup>2</sup> = 2(PT<sup>2</sup> + QT<sup>2</sup>)", "PQ<sup>2</sup> + PR<sup>2</sup> = 2(PT<sup>2</sup> - QR<sup>2</sup>)", "PQ<sup>2</sup> + PR = PT<sup>2</sup> + QT<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>In any triangle, the following relationship holds when a median is drawn from a vertex to the midpoint of the opposite side:</p><p>PQ&#178; + PR&#178; = 2(PT&#178; + QT&#178;)</p><p>This formula is derived from the median theorem, which states that the sum of the squares of the two sides of a triangle (PQ and PR) is equal to twice the sum of the square of the median (PT) and the square of half the base (QT), i.e., the length of the segment from P to the midpoint of QR.</p><p>The correct answer is: PQ&#178; + PR&#178; = 2(PT&#178; + QT&#178;)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In any triangle, the following relationship holds when a median is drawn from a vertex to the midpoint of the opposite side:</p><p>PQ&#178; + PR&#178; = 2(PT&#178; + QT&#178;)</p><p>This formula is derived from the median theorem, which states that the sum of the squares of the two sides of a triangle (PQ and PR) is equal to twice the sum of the square of the median (PT) and the square of half the base (QT), i.e., the length of the segment from P to the midpoint of QR.</p><p>The correct answer is: PQ&#178; + PR&#178; = 2(PT&#178; + QT&#178;)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the first 20 overs of a 50 over cricket match the run rate per over is 5.5. If the team has to chase a target of 310 in 50 overs then what should be the minimum run-rate in the remaining overs?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>50 &#2323;&#2357;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2350;&#2376;&#2330; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; 20 &#2323;&#2357;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2323;&#2357;&#2352; &#2352;&#2344; &#2352;&#2375;&#2335; 5.5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 50 &#2323;&#2357;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 310 &#2352;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2331;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2323;&#2357;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2352;&#2344;-&#2352;&#2375;&#2335; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["6.77", "6.55", "6.22", "6.66"], "options_hi": ["6.75", "6.25", "6.20", "6.67"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Total runs scored in the 1<sup>st</sup> 20 overs = (5.5  X  20) = 110</p><p>Now remaining runs that the team has to score in the remaining 30 overs = (310  -  110)= 200</p><p>Therefore, required run rate for the remaining overs = 200/30</p><p>= 6.66</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total runs scored in the 1<sup>st</sup> 20 overs = (5.5  X  20) = 110</p><p>Now remaining runs that the team has to score in the remaining 30 overs = (310  -  110)= 200</p><p>Therefore, required run rate for the remaining overs = 200/30</p><p>= 6.66</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>An inlet pipe fills a tank in 15 h. When filling, two leaks at the bottom, one emptying in 40 h and the other in 60 h, are left open. How long will it take to fill the tank completely?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2311;&#2344;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 15 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2349;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351;, &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2354;&#2368;&#2325; &#2326;&#2369;&#2354;&#2375; &#2352;&#2361; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2319;&#2325; 40 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; 60 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["30 h", "40 h", "50 h", "60 h"], "options_hi": ["30 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "40 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "50 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "60 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Rate of inlet = 1/15</p><p>Rate of leak 1 = &#8722;1/40</p><p>Rate of leak 2 = &#8722;1/60</p><p>Net rate = 1/15 &#8722;1/40 &#8722;1/60 = (8&#8722;3&#8722;2)/120 = 3/120 = 1/40</p><p>Time = 1/(1/40) = 40 h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Rate of inlet = 1/15</p><p>Rate of leak 1 = &#8722;1/40</p><p>Rate of leak 2 = &#8722;1/60</p><p>Net rate = 1/15 &#8722;1/40 &#8722;1/60 = (8&#8722;3&#8722;2)/120 = 3/120 = 1/40</p><p>Time = 1/(1/40) = 40 h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three straight lines - X, Y, and Z are parallel. &#8736;AOB = 78&deg;, and some other angles are shown in the given figure. What is the value of &#8736;OED?</p><p><img width=188 height=134 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24663/image003.png\" ></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368;&#2343;&#2368; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; - X, Y &#2324;&#2352; Z &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#8736;AOB = 78&deg; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#8736;OED &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=\"188\" height=\"134\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24663/image003.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["26&deg;", "30&deg;", "32&deg;", "28&deg;"], "options_hi": ["26&deg;", "30&deg;", "32&deg;", "28&deg;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=188 height=134 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24663/image003.png\" ></p><p>&#8736;EDC = 32&deg; [opposite Angle]</p><p>&#8736;BAD = 180&deg;  -  136&deg; = 44&deg; [Straight line]</p><p>&#8736;ODC = 44&deg; [Alternate angle]</p><p>&#8736;COD = 78&deg; [Opposite Angle]</p><p>&#8736;ODE = 32&deg; + 44&deg; = 76&deg;</p><p>In &#8710; EOD,</p><p>&#8736;OED = 180&deg;  -  76&deg;  -  78&deg; = 26&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=188 height=134 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24663/image003.png\" ></p><p>&#8736;EDC = 32&deg; [opposite Angle]</p><p>&#8736;BAD = 180&deg;  -  136&deg; = 44&deg; [Straight line]</p><p>&#8736;ODC = 44&deg; [Alternate angle]</p><p>&#8736;COD = 78&deg; [Opposite Angle]</p><p>&#8736;ODE = 32&deg; + 44&deg; = 76&deg;</p><p>In &#8710; EOD,</p><p>&#8736;OED = 180&deg;  -  76&deg;  -  78&deg; = 26&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>The area of the base of a rectangular tank is 720 m<sup>2</sup> and the volume of water contained in it is 28800 m<sup>3</sup>. What is the depth of the water?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 720 m<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; 28800 m<sup>3 </sup>&#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2361;&#2352;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["30 m", "40 m", "50 m", "60 m"], "options_hi": ["30 m", "40 m", "50 m", "60 m"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the length, width, and height of the rectangular tank is 'l' m, 'b' m, and 'h' m respectively.</p><p>Area of base of rectangular tank = lb = 720</p><p>Volume of rectangular tank = lbh = 28800</p><p>720h = 28800</p><p>h = 40 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the length, width, and height of the rectangular tank is 'l' m, 'b' m, and 'h' m respectively.</p><p>Area of base of rectangular tank = lb = 720</p><p>Volume of rectangular tank = lbh = 28800</p><p>720h = 28800</p><p>h = 40 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The LCM of x<sup>2</sup> &#8722; 8x + 15 and x<sup>2</sup> &#8722; 5x + 6 is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>x<sup>2</sup> &#8722; 8x + 15 &#2324;&#2352; x<sup>2</sup> &#8722; 5x + 6 &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["(x - 2) (x - 3) (x &#8722; 5)", "(x &#8722; 6)<sup>2</sup> (x + 1) (x &#8722; 3)", "(x &#8722; 6) (x + 1) (x &#8722; 3)", "(x + 6) (x + 1) (x &#8722; 3)"], "options_hi": ["(x - 2) (x - 3) (x &#8722; 5)", "(x &#8722; 6)<sup>2</sup> (x + 1) (x &#8722; 3)", "(x &#8722; 6) (x + 1) (x &#8722; 3)", "(x + 6) (x + 1) (x &#8722; 3)"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Factors of x<sup>2</sup> - 8x+15 = (x-3) (x-5)</p><p>Factors of x<sup>2</sup>&#8722;5x+6 = (x-3) (x-2)</p><p>LCM = (x-2) (x-3) (x-5)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Factors of x<sup>2</sup> - 8x+15 = (x-3) (x-5)</p><p>Factors of x<sup>2</sup>&#8722;5x+6 = (x-3) (x-2)</p><p>LCM = (x-2) (x-3) (x-5)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>Suman, Rani And Divya together invested Rs.55341. At the end of the year Suman receives Rs.2355, Rani receives Rs.3532.5 and Divya receives Rs.4239 as profit. What was the difference between the investment of Suman and Divya?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2360;&#2369;&#2350;&#2344;, &#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2352;&#2369;.55341 &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2369;&#2350;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &#2352;&#2369;.2355, &#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2352;&#2369;.3532.5 &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2352;&#2369;.4239 &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2369;&#2350;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2341;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.10296", "Rs.7000", "Rs.10000", "Rs.10600"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.10296", "&#2352;&#2369;.7000", "&#2352;&#2369;.10000", "&#2352;&#2369;.10600"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "\"<p>Ratio of their respective profits = 2355 : 3532.5 : 4239</p><p>= 10 : 15 : 18</p><p>So ratio of their investment = 10 : 15 : 18</p><p>Difference b/w the investment of Suman &amp; Divya = (18 &#8211; 10) = 8 units</p><p> &#8756; Required Difference = <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000655.png\"/> </p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p>Ratio of their respective profits = 2355 : 3532.5 : 4239</p><p>= 10 : 15 : 18</p><p>So ratio of their investment = 10 : 15 : 18</p><p>Difference b/w the investment of Suman &amp; Divya = (18 &#8211; 10) = 8 units</p><p> &#8756; Required Difference = <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000655.png\"/> </p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following fractions is nearest to 23/31?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>0.32<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">64", "options_en": ["27/39", "15/28", "22/29", "17/22"], "options_hi": ["816/2475", "812/2475", "808/2475", "820/2475"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>23/31 = 0.74</p><p>(a) 27/39 = 0.69</p><p>(b) 15/28 = 0.53</p><p>(c) 22/29 = 0.758 [Nearest]</p><p>(d) 17/22 = 0.77</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>23/31 = 0.74</p><p>(a) 27/39 = 0.69</p><p>(b) 15/28 = 0.53</p><p>(c) 22/29 = 0.758 [Nearest]</p><p>(d) 17/22 = 0.77</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">a", "q_hi": "<p><div>&nbsp;&#2351;&#2342;&#2367;&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">a", "options_en": ["3", "0", "2", "-3"], "options_hi": ["3", "0", "2", "-3"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>a/b + b/a = 1</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = ab ----(1)</p><p>Now,</p><p>(a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup>)/3ab = (a + b)( a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>  -  ab)/3ab</p><p>= (a + b)(ab  -  ab)/3ab</p><p>= 0</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a/b + b/a = 1</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = ab ----(1)</p><p>Now,</p><p>(a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup>)/3ab = (a + b)( a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>  -  ab)/3ab</p><p>= (a + b)(ab  -  ab)/3ab</p><p>= 0</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A takes 5 minutes and 40 seconds while B takes 6 minutes to complete a race. A beat B by 90 meters in the race if both start simultaneously from the starting point. Find the length of the course.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 5 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; B &#2325;&#2379; 6 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2340;&#2379; A, B &#2325;&#2379; 90 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1680 meters", "160 meters", "1620 meters", "1660 meters"], "options_hi": ["1680 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "160 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "1620 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "1660 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Time taken by A = 5 * 60 + 40 = 340 seconds</p><p>Time taken by B = 6 * 60 = 360 seconds</p><p>B cover distance in 20 seconds = 90</p><p>B cover distance in 360 seconds = 360 * 90/20</p><p>= 1620 meters</p><p>Hence, the length of the course = 1620 meters</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Time taken by A = 5 * 60 + 40 = 340 seconds</p><p>Time taken by B = 6 * 60 = 360 seconds</p><p>B cover distance in 20 seconds = 90</p><p>B cover distance in 360 seconds = 360 * 90/20</p><p>= 1620 meters</p><p>Hence, the length of the course = 1620 meters</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;Evaluate:&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">cos A[(1 - cot A)cot A + cosec<sup>2</sup> A]", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;: &nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">cos A[(1 - cot A)cot A + cosec<sup>2</sup> A]", "options_en": ["sinA", "1", "tanA", "2"], "options_hi": ["sinA", "1", "tanA", "2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=227 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18579/image027.png\"></p><p><img width=227 height=64 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18579/image028.png\"></p><p><img width=221 height=69 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18579/image029.png\"></p><p><img width=179 height=59 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18579/image030.png\"></p><p><img width=111 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18579/image031.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18579/image032.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=227 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18579/image027.png\"></p><p><img width=227 height=64 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18579/image028.png\"></p><p><img width=221 height=69 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18579/image029.png\"></p><p><img width=179 height=59 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18579/image030.png\"></p><p><img width=111 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18579/image031.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18579/image032.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<div>&nbsp;The value of <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>(1.38 + 9.5)<sup>2</sup> + (1.38 - 9.5)<sup>2</sup>", "q_hi": "<p><div><div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>(1.38 + 9.5)<sup>2</sup> + (1.38 - 9.5)<sup>2</sup>", "options_en": ["0.2", "2", "0.02", "200"], "options_hi": ["0.2", "2", "0.02", "200"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=184 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18799/image013.png\"></p><p><img width=388 height=60 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18799/image014.png\"></p><p><img width=197 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18799/image015.png\"></p><p><img width=47 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18799/image016.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=184 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18799/image013.png\"></p><p><img width=388 height=60 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18799/image014.png\"></p><p><img width=197 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18799/image015.png\"></p><p><img width=47 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18799/image016.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>A zookeeper counted a total of 80 heads in an enclosure. Upon checking, he found that there were 220 legs. If the only animals present were kangaroos and parrots, where each kangaroo had four legs and each parrot had two, how many kangaroos were in the enclosure?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2367;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2328;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2326;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 80 &#2360;&#2367;&#2352; &#2327;&#2367;&#2344;&#2375;&#2404; &#2332;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; 220 &#2346;&#2376;&#2352; &#2341;&#2375;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2306;&#2327;&#2366;&#2352;&#2370; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2368; &#2350;&#2380;&#2332;&#2370;&#2342; &#2341;&#2375;, &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2325;&#2306;&#2327;&#2366;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352; &#2341;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2340;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352; &#2341;&#2375;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2306;&#2327;&#2366;&#2352;&#2370; &#2341;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["30", "50", "40", "60"], "options_hi": ["30", "50", "40", "60"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Number of heads = number of kangaroos + number of parrots</p><p>Let number of parrots be X.</p><p>Then number of kangaroos be (80  -  X).</p><p>Total number of legs = 220</p><p>2X + 4(80  -  X) = 220</p><p>2X + 320  -  4X = 220</p><p>2X = 100</p><p>X = 50</p><p>Number of kangaroos = 80  -  50 = 30</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of heads = number of kangaroos + number of parrots</p><p>Let number of parrots be X.</p><p>Then number of kangaroos be (80  -  X).</p><p>Total number of legs = 220</p><p>2X + 4(80  -  X) = 220</p><p>2X + 320  -  4X = 220</p><p>2X = 100</p><p>X = 50</p><p>Number of kangaroos = 80  -  50 = 30</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Number of students who have given CHSL exam from institute A are what percentage of number of students who have given CPO exam from institute B?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2306;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; A &#2360;&#2375; CHSL &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; B &#2360;&#2375; CPO &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["113.25%", "127.5%", "118.75%", "124.5%"], "options_hi": ["113.25%", "127.5%", "118.75%", "124.5%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Number of students who have given CHSL exam from institute A = 1800 * 17/100 = 18 * 17</p><p>Number of students who have given CPO exam from institute B = 1600 * 15/100 = 16 * 15</p><p>Required% = (18 * 17) * 100/ (16 * 15) = 1275/10 = 127.5%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of students who have given CHSL exam from institute A = 1800 * 17/100 = 18 * 17</p><p>Number of students who have given CPO exam from institute B = 1600 * 15/100 = 16 * 15</p><p>Required% = (18 * 17) * 100/ (16 * 15) = 1275/10 = 127.5%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p> A man borrows a certain money from a bank and promise to pay the amount in two equal annual Instalments at the rate of 12.5% per annum compounded annually. If the total interest paid by him was Rs.7020. Find total principal. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2342;&#2350;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; 12.5% &#8203;&#8203;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; 7020 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2341;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2343;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["21870", "36720", "32840", "34640"], "options_hi": ["21870", "36720", "32840", "34640"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>R = 12.5% = 1/8</p><p>T = 2yrs.</p><p>We have,</p><p>Principal Instalment</p><p>8&#215;9 ---> 9 &#215; 9</p><p>(8) <sup>2</sup> ---> (9) <sup>2</sup></p><p>Total principal = 64 + 72 = 136</p><p>Total value of instalment = 81 &#215; 2 = 162</p><p>Int. paid = 162 &#8211; 136 = 26</p><p>A/q, 26 = 7020</p><p>= 1 x 7020/26 = 270</p><p>Each Instalment = 81 &#215; 270</p><p>= 21870</p><p>Total principal = 136 &#215; 270 = 36720 \"</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>R = 12.5% = 1/8</p><p>T = 2yrs.</p><p>We have,</p><p>Principal Instalment</p><p>8&#215;9 ---> 9 &#215; 9</p><p>(8) <sup>2</sup> ---> (9) <sup>2</sup></p><p>Total principal = 64 + 72 = 136</p><p>Total value of instalment = 81 &#215; 2 = 162</p><p>Int. paid = 162 &#8211; 136 = 26</p><p>A/q, 26 = 7020</p><p>= 1 x 7020/26 = 270</p><p>Each Instalment = 81 &#215; 270</p><p>= 21870</p><p>Total principal = 136 &#215; 270 = 36720 \"</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}]}